Feature: applyexact
  apply removes the entries of exact directories that the source state does not manage.

  Background:
    Given an empty home directory
    And the source state manages:
      | target       | kind  | contents                 |
      | ~/.dir       | exact |                          |
      | ~/.dir/file1 | file  | # contents of .dir/file1 |
    And the home directory contains:
      | target            | kind | contents                      |
      | ~/.dir/file1      | file | # contents of .dir/file1      |
      | ~/.dir/file2      | file | # contents of .dir/file2      |
      | ~/.dir/subdir/file | file | # contents of .dir/subdir/file |

  # archive files:
  #   golden/file3
